    {
        "content": "<p>it's not clear to me why we should choose <code>ite_prop_iff_and</code> over its dual <code>ite_prop_iff_or</code></p>",
        "id": 604900282,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1781878288
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Should.20ite_prop_iff_and.20be.20.40.5Bsimp.5D.3F/near/604900282\">said</a> :</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>it's not clear to me why we should choose <code>ite_prop_iff_and</code> over its dual <code>ite_prop_iff_or</code></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>one answer is because maybe we can't have both, but I will look into what the difference is</p>\n<p>Do you know advantages to each <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"816344\">@Aaron Liu</span> ?</p>",
        "id": 604917797,
        "sender_full_name": "Attila Vajda",
        "timestamp": 1781881905
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Should.20ite_prop_iff_and.20be.20.40.5Bsimp.5D.3F/near/604900282\">said</a> :</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>it's not clear to me why we should choose <code>ite_prop_iff_and</code> over its dual <code>ite_prop_iff_or</code></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I am learning about this, it's fun<br>\nthey are interchangeable as propositions,<br>\nDe Morgan duals of each other,<br>\nbut maybe aren't symmetric for simp</p>\n<p>the situation is perhaps similar to how in tableaux (proof trees)<br>\n∧ doesn't branch while ∨ branches, and prioritising non-branching<br>\nformulas on the tree results in a simpler tree</p>\n<p>when we put <code>@[simp]</code> on <code>_and</code>,<br>\nsimp creates a canonical-ish form,<br>\nit takes</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and rewrites it to</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">¬</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>then <span aria-label=\"ocean\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f30a\" role=\"img\" title=\"ocean\">:ocean:</span>flow is something like:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">goal</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">¬</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">goal1</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">goal2</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">¬</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">¬</span><span class=\"n\">P</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which might be great to:<br>\n<code>constructor</code>; then assume <code>P</code> or <code>¬P</code>.</p>\n<p>when we put <code>@[simp]</code> on _or,<br>\nsimp outputs a branching (non-canonical-ish?) form,<br>\ntakes<br>\n<code>⊢ if P then Q else R</code></p>\n<p>returns<br>\n⊢(P∧Q) ∨ (¬P∧R)</p>\n<p>where<br>\nyou cannot use constructor,<br>\n∵ there isn't a deterministic split<br>\nso you have to choose a side:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">left</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">🌿</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">right</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">🌿</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">¬</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">¬</span><span class=\"n\">P</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>then flow is:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">goal</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∨</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">¬</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">left</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OR</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">right</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NON</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">DETERMINISTIC</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">choice</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">split</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">again</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which might be less useful for goals,<br>\nbut is better for a hypothesis on LHS:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>rewriting <code>h</code> to</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∨</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">¬</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>then rcases (<a href=\"http://ite_prop_iff_or.mp\">ite_prop_iff_or.mp</a> h).</p>\n<p>so</p>\n<ul>\n<li>goal/prove ⇒ <code>_and</code> is ergonomic</li>\n<li>hypothesis/use ⇒ <code>_or</code> is ergonomic</li>\n</ul>\n<p>_and is invertible<br>\n_or is non-invertible</p>\n<p>there are other reasons too, for putting @[simp] on _and, eg</p>\n<p>_or → _and<br>\nconstructive floor<br>\n<code>_and → _or</code><br>\ngenerally not constructive</p>\n<p>also don't have both, because then you get same LHS with two RHS</p>\n<p>this pattern is perhaps the very similar for dite lemmas,<br>\nso it might worth implementing together:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">on</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"ss\">`ite_prop_iff_and</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">on</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"ss\">`dite_prop_iff_and</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/attilavjda/silver-octo-carnival/blob/main/ite_prop_iff/ite_dite.md\">more on this here</a></p>\n<p>What do you think?</p>",
        "id": 605741017,
        "sender_full_name": "Attila Vajda",
        "timestamp": 1782138451
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>you wouldn't be using <code>cases</code> or <code>constructor</code> after a <code>simp</code> anyways because that would be a non-terminal simp</p>",
        "id": 605881509,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1782173071
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>We generally avoid <code>simp</code> lemmas that duplicate a subexpression - if <code>P</code> is a long expression, this lemma would be unwieldy</p>",
        "id": 606580872,
        "sender_full_name": "Ruben Van de Velde",
        "timestamp": 1782418241
    }
]